{#
	What the head says about the page: its description on every page, and only where a page sets them
	its canonical address, a robots rule, the Open Graph tags with a share picture, X's card, the site
	verification codes (the home page) and its structured data (a public page; owner, 2026-11-06). A
	course landing page's ADMIN preview asks not to be indexed and claims no address. ThemeRenderer builds
	meta from the page's page_meta (Search\PageMetadata); every bundled theme includes this in its head in
	place of a description of its own.
#}
{# Says, before anything is drawn, that this browser runs scripts, so a narrow screen's menu is folded behind its Menu button
   from the first paint instead of folding when the script arrives and moving the page up (the SEO brief's Core Web Vitals,
   2026-11-09: it was most of the home page's layout shift). Without scripts nothing is set and the whole menu shows. #}
<script>document.documentElement.dataset.clScript = '1';</script>
{% set head_meta = meta|default({description: 'Structured self-study courses, progress tracking and assessments.', canonical: '', robots: '', og: {}}) %}
<meta name="description" content="{{ head_meta.description }}">
{% if head_meta.robots %}<meta name="robots" content="{{ head_meta.robots }}">{% endif %}
{% if head_meta.canonical %}<link rel="canonical" href="{{ head_meta.canonical }}">{% endif %}
{% if head_meta.og %}{% for property, content in head_meta.og %}<meta property="og:{{ property }}" content="{{ content }}">{% endfor %}<meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ app_name|default('') }}">{% endif %}
{% if head_meta.twitter_card|default('') %}<meta name="twitter:card" content="{{ head_meta.twitter_card }}">{% endif %}
{% for verification_name, verification_code in head_meta.verification|default({}) %}<meta name="{{ verification_name }}" content="{{ verification_code }}">{% endfor %}
{% include '@platform/partials/structured-data.html.twig' %}
